# local env files
.env*.local

# Every other .env variant — backups above all.
#
# `.gitignore` covered the exact name `.env` and `.env*.local`, and nothing else. A
# backup of the production env taken during the fitment rollout
# (`.env.backup-20260907T191201Z`, holding the real Saleor token, the garage cookie
# secret and the Stripe keys) therefore sat in the working tree matched by no rule at
# all, one `git add -A` away from a commit.
#
# This repository is a PUBLIC fork of `saleor/storefront` (CLAUDE.md §10.1). A commit
# pushed anywhere in a fork network stays reachable by its SHA from every repo in that
# network, permanently — deleting the branch, rewriting history or making the repo
# private do not undo it. The only remedy would be to revoke and rotate every key.
#
# `.env.example` is tracked on purpose and stays tracked.
.env.*
!.env.example

